VALUES (NULL, NULL, 125, 'Diablo', 'Diablo', 'game', 1996, 'https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co3ggo.jpg', 'https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_1080p/ar699o.jpg', 'Diablo is an isometric strategy RPG and one of the most well-known examples of the action-RPG subgenre. Although some of the game mechanics resemble a typical RPG, all actions are done in real-time just like in an action game. The player have to kill hordes of monsters through randomized dungeon levels in order to gain experience points, gold and a variety of equipment to bolster the hero''s monster-killing potency.', 'https://www.igdb.com/games/diablo', '["PC (Microsoft Windows)", "Mac", "PlayStation"]', NULL, 8.4, 0, 1.06, '2026-11-22 03:06:26', '2026-11-22 03:06:26')
